# W13: the updater end to end, against the release feed the rig hosts on loopback (--update). The
# feed's version is newer than this build's, so the app checks at once, downloads, verifies the
# SHA-256 and replaces the stand-in AppImage in the run's data directory; "Restart to update" asks
# the app's restart seam (the rig records it and starts nothing). No release is contacted and no
# file outside the run's data directory is touched.

app 1280 800
click auth-connect
wait core label "Username" within 5
click auth-username
type "alexk"
click auth-password
type "hunter2"
click auth-login
wait core session signed-in
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core connection connected

# The check starts with the app; the card appears once the file is verified and in place.
wait core w13 state ready within 20
wait core w13 banner 9.9.9 within 5
wait core w13 appimage updated within 5
wait idle
shot 01-update-ready

# The same news, and the manual check, in the settings.
navigate /settings
wait core route settings
click settings-tab-desktop
wait core element desktop-update-status
wait idle
shot 02-update-settings

# "Check for updates" asks the feed again (the first check was the start-up one).
expect core w13 checks 1
click desktop-check-updates
wait core w13 checks 2 within 10
wait core w13 state ready within 10

# "Restart to update" through the seam.
click update-restart
wait core w13 restart-asked 1 within 5

# Dismissing the card is per version, and remembered.
click update-dismiss
wait core w13 banner none within 5
expect settings /dismissed_update "9.9.9"
